---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import NavBar from '../components/NavBar.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="How to Use Terraform cidrsubnet() Function | VPC Subnet Planning | DevSubnet"
  description="Complete guide to using Terraform's cidrsubnet() function for VPC subnet planning. Calculate subnet offsets, avoid CIDR overlaps, and generate production-ready HCL code for AWS, Azure, and GCP multi-AZ architectures."
>
  <div class="app-shell">
    <NavBar path='guide' />

    <main class="page-main">
      <div class="content-container">
        <!-- Breadcrumb -->
        <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/">Home</a> <span class="sep">/</span> <strong>How to Use Terraform cidrsubnet()</strong>
        </nav>

        <section class="page-header">
          <div class="eyebrow">TERRAFORM HCL</div>
          <h1>How to Use Terraform cidrsubnet()</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            Terraform&rsquo;s <code>cidrsubnet()</code> function generates a subnet CIDR from a parent prefix, a number of extra bits, and a subnet index. Learn the signature, common patterns, and the mistakes that cause overlap bugs.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="page-body">
          <div class="text-block">
            <h2>The Function Signature</h2>
            <div class="code-block">
              <pre><code>cidrsubnet(prefix, newbits, netnum)</code></pre>
            </div>
            <ul class="step-list">
              <li><strong>prefix</strong> &mdash; the parent CIDR block, e.g. <code>"10.0.0.0/16"</code>.</li>
              <li><strong>newbits</strong> &mdash; how many extra bits to add to the prefix length. Adding 8 to a <code>/16</code> creates <code>/24</code> subnets.</li>
              <li><strong>netnum</strong> &mdash; the zero-based index of the subnet. 0 = first subnet, 1 = second, and so on.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              The result is a complete CIDR string you can place directly into a subnet resource.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="text-block">
            <h2>Worked Example</h2>
            <div class="code-block">
              <pre><code>cidrsubnet("10.0.0.0/16", 8, 0) # =&gt; 10.0.0.0/24
cidrsubnet("10.0.0.0/16", 8, 1) # =&gt; 10.0.1.0/24
cidrsubnet("10.0.0.0/16", 8, 255) # =&gt; 10.0.255.0/24</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p>
              With <code>newbits = 8</code> the <code>/16</code> is carved into 256 <code>/24</code> subnets, and <code>netnum</code> picks which one. This is why looping over Availability Zones feels natural &mdash; each zone simply gets a sequential index.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="text-block">
            <h2>Typical Multi-AZ Pattern</h2>
            <div class="code-block">
              <pre><code>variable "vpc_cidr" &#123; default = "10.0.0.0/16" &#125;

locals &#123;
  azs = ["us-east-1a", "us-east-1b", "us-east-1c"]
&#125;

resource "aws_subnet" "public" &#123;
  count             = length(local.azs)
  vpc_id            = aws_vpc.main.id
  availability_zone = local.azs[count.index]
  cidr_block        = cidrsubnet(var.vpc_cidr, 8, count.index)
&#125;

resource "aws_subnet" "private" &#123;
  count             = length(local.azs)
  vpc_id            = aws_vpc.main.id
  availability_zone = local.azs[count.index]
  cidr_block        = cidrsubnet(var.vpc_cidr, 8, length(local.azs) + count.index)
&#125;</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p>
              Private subnets use a different offset (<code>length(azs) + index</code>) so public and private ranges never collide. For most workloads a <code>/16</code> VPC with <code>/24</code> subnets is a safe, scalable default.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="text-block">
            <h2>Common Pitfalls</h2>
            <ul class="step-list">
              <li><strong>Exceeding the child count.</strong> <code>netnum</code> must stay below 2<sup>newbits</sup>. With <code>newbits = 8</code> the valid indexes are 0&ndash;255 only.</li>
              <li><strong>Not enough space.</strong> Subnets must fit the host count. A <code>/26</code> gives only 62 usable hosts &mdash; choosing it for 100-instance autoscaling groups fails at deploy time.</li>
              <li><strong>Reusing the same offset.</strong> Forgetting to offset a second resource type creates silently overlapping subnets in the same route table.</li>
              <li><strong>Ignoring cloud reservations.</strong> AWS keeps 5 IPs per subnet, Azure 5, GCP 4. Size ranges with the provider rule, not the raw 2<sup>h</sup> &minus; 2.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="tips-box">
            <h3>Prefer cidrsubnets() for Many Blocks</h3>
            <p>
              When you need several same-size blocks at once, the plural <code>cidrsubnets(prefix, result_cidrs...)&rarr;</code> variant returns a list directly: <code>cidrsubnets("10.0.0.0/16", 8, 8, 8)</code> produces three <code>/24</code>s. It keeps offsets out of your hands entirely.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <div class="try-tool">
          <a href="/terraform-subnet-planner" class="btn-return">Try the Terraform Subnet Planner &rarr;</a>
        </div>

        <div class="related-tools">
          <h3>Related Tools</h3>
          <div class="tools-grid">
            <a href="/terraform-subnet-planner">Terraform Subnet Planner</a>
            <a href="/aws-vpc-subnet-calculator">AWS VPC Calculator</a>
            <a href="/azure-vnet-subnet-calculator">Azure VNet Calculator</a>
            <a href="/gcp-vpc-subnet-calculator">GCP VPC Calculator</a>
            <a href="/kubernetes-subnet-planner">K8s Subnet Planner</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="page-cta">
          <a href="/" class="btn-return">← Return to Calculator</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <span>DEVSUBNET.COM / ENGINEERED FOR CLEAR NETWORKS</span>
      <div class="footer-links">
        <a href="/about">About Us</a>
        <a href="/contact">Contact</a>
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
        <a href="/terms">Terms & Conditions</a>
        <a href="/faq">FAQ</a>
      </div>
      <span>NO DATA LEAVES YOUR DEVICE</span>
    </footer>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-main { flex: 1; padding: 3rem 1.5rem 5rem; }
  .content-container { max-width: 54rem; margin: 0 auto; text-align: left; }

  .breadcrumb { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 2rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .breadcrumb a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .breadcrumb .sep { color: var(--text-secondary); }

  .page-header { margin-bottom: 3rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color); padding-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .page-header .eyebrow { font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .page-header h1 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary); letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.1; }
  .page-header .lede { font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65; max-width: 40rem; margin: 0; }

  .page-body { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3rem; }
  .text-block h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 1rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .text-block p { font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .text-block p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .text-block code { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; font-size: 0.85rem; background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: 0.1em 0.4em; border-radius: 4px; color: var(--accent); }

  .step-list { margin: 0 0 1rem; padding-left: 1.5rem; }
  .step-list li { font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }

  .code-block { background: var(--bg-secondary, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03)); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; overflow-x: auto; }
  .code-block pre { margin: 0; }
  .code-block code { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--accent); background: none; padding: 0; }

  .tips-box { background: var(--card-bg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03)); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 1.5rem 2rem; }
  .tips-box h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 0.75rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .tips-box p { font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0; }

  .try-tool { margin-top: 3rem; }

  .related-tools { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color); }
  .related-tools h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .tools-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(150px, 1fr)); gap: 0.75rem; }
  .tools-grid a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .tools-grid a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  .page-cta { margin-top: 3rem; }
  .btn-return { display: inline-block; background: var(--text-primary); color: var(--bg-primary); padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem; border-radius: var(--radius-full); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.875rem; text-decoration: none; transition: opacity var(--transition-fast); }
  .btn-return:hover { opacity: 0.85; }
</style>